# Indeed we did. Oslo we reached 4 other suppliers, Bergen 2, and Fredrikstad 1.
# For context, the market is sparse of good suppliers (we already had 2 in 9 months of ops), this why 15 days is essential to give us the flexibility to move fast and avoid getting stuck one full month with bad or uncompliant providers;
# That being said, our choice went for 3 providers with whom we already had an indirect commercial relationship. These were Jacob AS subcontractors with whom we terminated amicably some weeks ago;
# In it, Jacob AS waved clause 7.4 (NCC). This basically meant that we were entitled to engage with his own suppliers without having to pay a fee;
# Because these contractors already worked for us, they are already acquainted with our operational processes meaning that the learning curve was reduced to zero as opposed to onboard a new 3pl and spend extra time and resources training new drivers;
# Their performance is attested and this was my main criteria, alongside price, to signed them in. 
# We managed to negotiate the best market prices (in Oslo the average unit charging cost dropped from 5.5nok to 3.4nok);
# Our experience with Jacob proofed the opposite - giving too much power to one supplier in the market almost damaged our operations (Hannah can give you the context).

