h3. Summary

h4. Conclusions made based on the research done:

* There is no evidence that shorter articles deflect better than longer articles.

{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}
*A/B test ideas:*

* to test short and longer version of the same article (the components or additional information that make the article longer should be defined for each article separately)
* to check how subheading and text division into subsections affect the readability instead of short/long article (i.e. how the information is searchable within the text regardless of its length)
{panel}

* There is no evidence that the deflection rate is higher for articles with a better readability score

{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}
*Further research idea*:

* to check common words rate or other metrics instead of readability score because the readability score is based on the number of syllables, words, and sentences in the text (i.e. text structure).
{panel}

