From a policy perspective; 

We have been told that there will be a requirement from the city of Gothenburg that we provide a possibility to provide phone support in Swedish. This will be part of the agreement  which governs the conditions under which we operate in the city. This is said to be a non negoatiable requirement from the city and will apply equally.

As for more specific requirements we dont know yet since we yet havent seen the draft agreement from Gothenburg. However, what we know so far is that this will be applicable from July 1st 2021, Swedish speaking support is to be available office hours, no specific response times, no SLA. 

As for recording messages, this will rasie a few legal questions but I pressume that these already are covered in our ordninary phone support; 

* At least one of the parties to the call must know that the call is being recorded 
* informing the other person that the call is being recorded. 
* Personal data may be processed during a recorded conversation which brings it under GDPR, but agian, I pressume that this is already properly covered

