Here is a copy of an email as well. Formatting is poor, please refer to inbox email rather.

Hello Calum,Thank you for your  mail.I'll try to provide as much info as possible.
I have added some people into copy, so that they would be able to see my responses and provide more information, if they see applicable.
Before jumping to the answers I'd like to describe planned usage patterns for this product.Lets call them "cases":1. Mobile development team was asking for "tracing of everything", but only for internal employees and most likely with user consent. So here is where the "data" question comes from.2. We, Backend platform, would like to gather telemetry data. How much, how long, when, what is the sequence? No data/PII expected to occur here.3. \[Potential/Optional] We might find a product as good, that we could even debug live customers cases on the fly, but only with consent and most restrictive means we could apply.Without consent we don't even record stuff for cases 1 and 3. For case 2, I guess we don't need consent.


{quote}_1. Whose personal data is to be processed as part of the live tracing? e.g. staff from a specific territory or region, users falling within a business category? And has the sample type and size been determined proportionately?_
{quote}

With case 1 we'd assume only internal employees, who gave their consent that their data is going to be traced. Not sure, what exactly do you mean by sample? If you mean a group of people, then I guess it is already answered. If it is about data, then I'd say as much as possible, with some exceptions. The main risk here is user auth data abuse as well as payment data theft.




{quote}_2. What personal data is to be processed? Personal data is data that relates to an individual, something that identifies someone, or something that might help identify somebody with other pieces of data e.g. names, account IDs, location data etc._
{quote}

If we speak about case 1 and purpose of it - it is mostly about "creating better product" and debugging. But this includes basically all the data, what backend and mobile clients do share. 




{quote}_3. What do you reckon to be the other data that is being processed during the live tracing cycle? e.g. completion rates for in-App tasks, response timeliness._
{quote}

This is mostly about case 2. This data is anonymous. Telemetry data about single request as well as some high-level stats of the backend, e.g. call graphs and internal timings. I don't think there is something about in-app at all, with this solution we don't want to track screen clicks, screen time or something like this. It is mostly about data passing between backend and frontend, as well as specifics of communication.

{quote}
_4. Why are you collecting the data at (3) above? What's the purpose? What are you trying to achieve? What is the 'good' in it?_
{quote}

As we speak about telemetry mostly, it helps us identify communication bottlenecks with mobile clients, finding out what are the flows on the backend as well as their characteristics. This information would allow us to optimize overall communication flow and its performance.

{quote}
_5. Is live tracing novel? Or is it, indeed, an industry norm and well-established practice to achieve the purposes at (4)?_{quote}

It is not novel.

